WEBVTT

00:11:58.868 --> 00:12:00.413
You need both in life.

00:12:00.837 --> 00:12:01.993
Why do people do this?

00:12:02.017 --> 00:12:04.722
I'm going to quote
a molecular biologist, Sydney Brenner,

00:12:04.746 --> 00:12:06.629
who's 70 years old, so he can say this.

00:12:06.653 --> 00:12:09.866
He said, "It's always important
to distinguish between chastity

00:12:09.890 --> 00:12:11.114
and impotence."

00:12:11.500 --> 00:12:12.685
Now --

00:12:12.709 --> 00:12:14.812
(Laughter)

00:12:14.836 --> 00:12:20.646
I want to share with you
a little equation, OK?

00:12:20.670 --> 00:12:25.867
How does understanding science
and the arts fit into our lives

00:12:25.891 --> 00:12:27.046
and what's going on

00:12:27.070 --> 00:12:30.173
and the things we're talking about
here at the design conference?